1149-    """Cross-sectional relative-strength spread: daily P&L of a long/short
1150-    portfolio built from ranks across the collected universe.
1151-
1152-    At each date t >= lookback: compute each ticker's lookback return
1153-    (closes[i-lookback : i+1], past-only); rank tickers descending; long the
1154-    top_k, short the bottom_k with equal capital per leg; hold one day;
1155-    daily rebalance. The spread P&L at bar t equals the mean of the
1156-    long-legs' next-day simple returns minus the mean of the short-legs'
1157-    next-day simple returns. Bars before lookback, and days with fewer than
1158-    2*k tickers available, are neutral (P&L = 0).
1159-
1160-    No look-ahead: every input at bar t uses closes only up to and
1161-    including t; the realized P&L is the return realized between bar t
1162-    and bar t+1.
1163-
1164-    Args:
1165-        tickers: dict ticker -> BarSequence of adjusted closes (all tickers
1166-            share the same date grid).
1167-        lookback: lookback window in bars.
1168-        top_k, bottom_k: leg sizes.
1169-
1170-    Returns:
1171-        np.ndarray of daily spread P&L (simple returns), one entry per bar
1172-        (0.0 where no trade is possible).
1173-    """
1174-    min_len = min(len(tb) for tb in tickers.values())
1175-    daily_pnl = np.zeros(min_len, dtype=np.float64)
1176-    for i in range(lookback, min_len - 1):
